      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A new procedure of extracting data from measurements by single-probe radionuclide ventriculography is presented which reduces the phase differences during summation of single-beat actions and permits the use of a greater number of single actions for summation. Sum curves so determined are better suited for measurements of ejection fractions, compliance and ventricular blood flow rates."},
